AB  - Integrating large language models (LLMs) into academic infrastructure requires rigorous safety mechanisms. This paper presents a comparative evaluation of two guard models, Llama Guard 3 (with a Low-Rank Adaptation (LoRA) adapter) and GPT OSS Safeguard, in the context of securing an administrative chatbot at Warsaw University of Technology (WUT), incorporating a custom Topic Restriction category that enforces domain boundaries. Results reveal a fundamental tradeoff: Llama Guard 3 exhibits high recall and low classification latency, but at the cost of numerous false positives. GPT OSS Safeguard achieves higher precision and better threat categorization, yet its response time precludes synchronous deployment. The study also revealed a significant discrepancy between expert labels and user perception, underscoring the inherent subjectivity of safety classification.
