AB  - Generative AI chatbots are used in more and more fields, but until the technology can be secured and trusted, it remains sensitive to unauthorized access and adversarial prompts. This paper will use experimental approaches to improve the safety of chatbots by testing a new model, the SACD, that combines the use of SASE JEM authentication and the DeepFool adversarial defense. The framework will block errant or malicious users, and subsequently identify and counter opposing inputs, such that only harmless prompts are passed through the chatbot. The SACD framework performed well with using the LLM Jailbreak + Safety Data on Kaggle as the program provided a high-level of robustness, scoring 98% and decreasing the number of unsafe outputs and attack success rates significantly. These findings affirm the fact that the suggested structure offers a stable, multi -layered defense system, which integrates access-level protection with the model-level adversarial protection and therefore offers secure, trustworthy, and resilient chatbot interactions.
