AB  - Navigating university systems for course selection, schedule planning, and course availability often presents challenges for students, faculty, and advisors due to complex interfaces and filters. This paper introduces an AI-powered chatbot that enables users including students, faculty, and staff to query course offerings, scheduling details, section availability, and departmental listings using natural language. The system integrates institutional data from Ellucian Banner Student Information System (SIS) and supports multiple backend architectures, including star schema creation, direct SQL generation via few-shot prompting, feedback loops for query refinement, ThoughtSpot’s natural language search, conversational amendments, and embedding-based retrieval. We evaluate the effectiveness of these approaches through representative use cases and compare them based on accuracy, flexibility, speed, and user satisfaction. Our results suggest that a hybrid solution combining these methods provides the most balanced performance and usability across diverse course discovery scenarios.
